list.item:
Aldrich, George H., Acting Deputy Legal
                                Adviser, Department of State, from January until October 1969;
                                Deputy Legal Adviser

Chafee, John H., Captain, USN;
                                Secretary of the Navy from January 31, 1969, until May 4,
                                1972

Froehlke, Robert F., Captain, USA;
                                Assistant Secretary of Defense for Administration from January 1969
                                until June 1971; Secretary of the Army from July 1, 1971

Harlow, Bryce N., Assistant to the
                                President for Congressional Relations from 1969 until 1970;
                                Counselor to the President from 1970

McCain, John S., Jr., Admiral, USN;
                                Commander in Chief, CINCPAC, from July 31, 1968, until September 1,
                                1972

person.note:
Assistant to the President for International Economic Affairs, and Executive
                    Director of the Council on International Economic Policy in 1971 and 1972;
                    Secretary of Commerce from January 27, 1972, until December 8, 1972

Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for Near East and South Asia, 1970;
                    Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for Policy Plans and National Security
                    Council Affairs, 1971

Assistant Director, Bureau of the Budget, from January 1969 until June 1970;
                    Assistant Director, Office of Management and Budget, from July 1970 until August
                    1971; Chairman of the Atomic Energy Commission from August 1971
